Article 51
Prevention efforts as referred to in Article 49 shall be carried out through:
a. communication, information, and education about the dangers for Children if involved in production and distribution as well as the dangers of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropics, and other addictive substances;
b. enhancement of the role of parents, families, the Community, educators, education personnel, religious leaders, customary leaders, Community leaders in supporting the Social Reintegration process of Children who are Victims of Narcotics, Alcohol, Psychotropics, and Other Addictive Substances Abuse;
c. provision of understanding and awareness to Children regarding the dangers of smoking;
d. provision of understanding and awareness to Children about the dangers of Children involved in production and distribution as well as the dangers of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropics, and other addictive substances;
e. involvement of Children as peers in order to provide understanding and change of mindset about the dangers of Children involved in production and distribution as well as the dangers of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropics, and other addictive substances; and
f. inclusion of anti-narcotics, alcohol, psychotropics, and other addictive substances teaching materials in education units.

Article 64
Prevention efforts as referred to in Article 62 shall be carried out in the form of:
a. formulating and implementing policies related to action plans on the prevention and handling of Children with HIV and AIDS;
b. health promotion to increase public knowledge about the benefits of early detection and transmission of HIV and AIDS as well as to increase the knowledge and responsibility of mothers, pregnant mothers, Children, and married couples;
c. preventing the transmission of HIV and AIDS from mother to Child; d. preventing Children from using narcotics;
e. early detection by providing HIV and AIDS tests to pregnant mothers in areas with widespread and concentrated HIV and AIDS endemics;
f. early detection by providing HIV and AIDS tests to pregnant mothers with sexually transmitted infections and tuberculosis in low HIV epidemic areas;
g. using sterile medical equipment for Children to avoid HIV and AIDS;
h. avoiding blood transfusions contaminated with HIV and AIDS to Children;
i. providing information about the transmission of HIV and AIDS to Children;
j. changing Children's behavior to avoid HIV and AIDS;
k. keeping Children away from making tattoos; and
l. establishing communication, consultation, and information centers on HIV and AIDS at the village level.

Article 73
