Article 47
The involvement of various companies, labor unions, non-governmental organizations, and the Community in the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children as referred to in Article 44 letter c is carried out through:
a. formulation of policies regarding the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children in their environment;
b. cooperation to prevent Children from being exploited economically and/or sexually;
c. campaigns for the elimination of economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children;
d. increased supervision to prevent Children from being exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. company support for the elimination of exploitation of Children through corporate social responsibility; and
f. reporting to the competent authorities if there is economic and/or sexual exploitation of Children.

Article 73
Prevention as referred to in Article 70 is carried out by means of:
a. involving the Community in carrying out Special Protection of Children;
b. increasing understanding related to kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking of Children;
c. establishing bilateral and multilateral cooperation, both national and international;
d. strengthening family resilience to prevent Children from kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking; and
e. increasing the responsibility of the Community, business sector, and mass media to protect Children from kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking.

